<!--
  ============================================================================
   POLICY 2 of 4 — Semantic caching
   (azure-openai-semantic-cache-lookup + azure-openai-semantic-cache-store)
  ============================================================================
   The point: an EXACT-match response cache almost never hits for chat — users
   phrase the same question a hundred different ways. Semantic cache embeds the
   incoming prompt, compares it (cosine similarity) to embeddings of previously
   answered prompts, and on a close-enough match returns the cached completion
   WITHOUT calling the model. Result: a paraphrased repeat costs ~0 tokens and
   returns in single-digit ms instead of a full generation round-trip.

   This is the "measure the cost/latency drop" demo: run a prompt, then run a
   reworded version of it, and watch the second one come back instantly with
   zero backend token spend.

   score-threshold is the MAX vector distance to count as a hit (lower = more
   similar required). 0.05 is tight; loosen toward ~0.2 to see more hits — but
   note the Learn warning that loose thresholds can surface stale/wrong answers.
   vary-by partitions the cache per subscription so tenants don't read each
   other's cached answers.

   Schema confirmed against Microsoft Learn azure-openai-semantic-cache-store-policy
   (updated 2026-02-24) and the paired lookup policy.

   VERIFY-IN-TEST (three real prerequisites):
     1. EXTERNAL CACHE: semantic cache needs an external cache wired to APIM
        (Azure Cache for Redis Enterprise w/ RediSearch). Developer SKU has a
        built-in cache for plain response-caching, but SEMANTIC cache requires the
        Redis Enterprise vector index. deploy-apim.sh leaves this OFF by default
        and prints how to add it — do it before this demo or lookups no-op.
     2. EMBEDDINGS BACKEND: embeddings-backend-id must point at an APIM backend
        that fronts a text-embedding-* deployment. We reference
        "openai-embeddings" — deploy-apim.sh can create an embeddings deployment
        + backend, OR you point it at an existing one. Confirm the embeddings
        model is available in your region.
     3. embeddings-backend-auth="system-assigned" => APIM's managed identity must
        have "Cognitive Services OpenAI User" on the embeddings account.
  ============================================================================
-->
<policies>
  <inbound>
    <base />
    <!-- BASE WIRING (required) — every demo policy must include these two
         elements, because `az apim api policy create` REPLACES the API-level
         policy (not layered). Without them, the API has no auth + no backend
         and every request returns HTTP 500. -->
    <set-backend-service backend-id="openai-pool" />
    <authentication-managed-identity resource="https://cognitiveservices.azure.com" />
    <!-- Try to answer from the semantic cache before touching the model. -->
    <azure-openai-semantic-cache-lookup
        score-threshold="0.05"
        embeddings-backend-id="openai-embeddings"
        embeddings-backend-auth="system-assigned">
      <vary-by>@(context.Subscription.Id)</vary-by>
    </azure-openai-semantic-cache-lookup>
    <!-- Microsoft's recommended guard: cap calls right after the cache lookup so
         a cache outage can't stampede the backend. -->
    <rate-limit calls="20" renewal-period="60" />
  </inbound>
  <backend>
    <base />
  </backend>
  <outbound>
    <!-- Store the freshly generated completion for future semantically-similar
         prompts. TTL 120s keeps the demo cache short-lived and obvious. -->
    <azure-openai-semantic-cache-store duration="120" />
    <base />
  </outbound>
  <on-error>
    <base />
  </on-error>
</policies>
